{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/def-monomial-basis","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:monomial-basis","kind":"definition","title":"Monomials and monomial bases","tags":["groebner-basis","monomial"],"leanRef":"ugb:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement","text":"monomial-basis.md","leanSource":"folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/monomial-basis.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:monomial-basis\"></a><p>Throughout, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code> is a commutative ring with unity and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> is an\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-algebra without quasi-zeros (i.e.\\ elements <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">a \\in A</code> such that\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">bac = 0</code> for all <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b, c \\in A</code> not both <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code>).</p>\n<p>Choose a set of algebra generators\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A = R\\langle x_i \\mid i \\in \\Lambda\\rangle</code> for some index set\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Lambda</code>.</p>\n<p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\alpha = \\alpha_1 \\alpha_2 \\cdots \\alpha_n</code> be a\nfinite-length word in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Lambda</code>. A <strong>monomial</strong> in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> is the ordered\nproduct</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  x_\\alpha := x_{\\alpha_1} \\cdot x_{\\alpha_2} \\cdots x_{\\alpha_n}.</code></pre>\n<p>Suppose <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> is free as an <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-module. We say <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code>\nhas a <strong>monomial basis</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">B</code> subordinate to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Lambda</code> if <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">B</code> is a subset\nof all finite-length words in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Lambda</code> such that</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  A = R\\{x_\\beta \\mid \\beta \\in B\\}.</code></pre>\n<p>We identify <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">x_\\beta</code> to simplify notation. The admissible subsets <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">B</code> are the <strong>monomial bases</strong> of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/monomial-basis.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Definition","number":"2.2.1"}
